WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
Meet Afterlight, a museum from twenty-one twenty-six.

2
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:12.662
Ordinary objects become strange little stories, with Sanity holding the
collection and a human curator deciding what goes on display.

3
00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:14.135
Start with a cassette.

4
00:00:14.135 --> 00:00:19.706
Rotate the original three-dimensional model, then compare what we can see
with its possible story.

5
00:00:19.706 --> 00:00:23.337
Observation and imagination stay separate.

6
00:00:23.337 --> 00:00:25.800
The curator can also upload an image.

7
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:30.291
Here, we're using a render of our own cup as the sample upload.

8
00:00:30.291 --> 00:00:35.015
It stays an image, never a pretend three-dimensional reconstruction.

9
00:00:35.015 --> 00:00:40.585
With consent, Gemini suggests a title, material, and visible details.

10
00:00:40.585 --> 00:00:42.685
These are marked unverified.

11
00:00:42.685 --> 00:00:46.309
They only enter the form when the curator chooses to use them.

12
00:00:46.315 --> 00:00:51.970
After saving the object to Sanity, we ask A I for a fictional
interpretation.

13
00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:54.846
We can edit the exhibition label before saving.

14
00:00:54.846 --> 00:00:59.337
Drafting cannot approve the object or change its observed details.

15
00:00:59.348 --> 00:01:01.678
Now we submit the draft for review.

16
00:01:01.678 --> 00:01:04.081
Approval is a separate curator action.

17
00:01:04.081 --> 00:01:08.002
Only then does the object become part of the public collection.

18
00:01:08.015 --> 00:01:14.944
Visitors can inspect the image and its story, then follow the recorded
journey from intake through drafting and approval.

19
00:01:14.944 --> 00:01:18.685
Those decisions live beside the content in Sanity.

20
00:01:18.685 --> 00:01:19.935
Need another review?

21
00:01:19.935 --> 00:01:22.690
Give a reason and return the exhibit to draft.

22
00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:27.195
It leaves the public gallery, while the decision history is retained.

23
00:01:27.195 --> 00:01:29.646
Explore the collection without signing in.

24
00:01:29.646 --> 00:01:33.008
Judges can use curator access to try the full workflow.

25
00:01:33.008 --> 00:01:34.088
Afterlight.

26
00:01:34.088 --> 00:01:38.153
Small things, long afterlives, and a human final say.
